so I produced a book filled with  illustrations there's one on page 16 and  17 of two boys standing looking up at a  huge wall that they're considering  climbing over and going on an adventure  and of all the illustrations in the book  this is sort of I think defining of my  life and I think it's the most exciting  one which is we all imagined brighter  futures and it's as if we're standing at  this wall we don't know how to get over  it we don't know how to get to the other  side we don't know how to get what we  want and to me it's the choice to climb  the wall it's the choice to find a way  around the wall that is what  distinguishes the innovators from  everybody else that's what distinguishes  the doers from everybody else it's what  distinguishes those who find what  they're looking for those who find  happiness but the purpose of the book is  to remind us that we cannot climb that  wall by ourselves that if we want to  find that brighter future if we want to  change our lot it is for us to find  someone who will go with us  so I'm someone who will catch us if we  fall down someone who will help us up  over the wall and it's these two kids  standing looking up over the wall what's  most important is that they're doing it  together  you
 

